/-!
# KIL4: the uniform level step `stepU`

A *shift template* `TSh m` fixes the active field `i`, the fraction `k/d` of the unit, its sign and
the rational controls `cs j = (p_j, q_j)` (control `j` is `p_j · q_j⁻¹ mod N`).  The template does
not mention the modulus `N`, the level or any volume.

`stepU m rX T` is one fixed program.  It reads

* `N` from `sQQ` (and `-N` from `sNQ`),
* `vol (P :: L :: A)` from the register `rX` (`rXs` or `rXb`),
* `vol B` from `rVB` and `vol Cs` from `rVC`,

builds the size parameters and the collapsed offset-table stages, computes every control
`p_j q_j⁻¹ mod N` at run time (`ctrlE`), and runs the uniform shift body.

`stepU_spec`: on the level layout `(hdLayout A B Cs m N).cons2 P L` it computes
`(T.eval N).arr`, the array action of the shift step the template denotes.
